.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/p-locate Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "p-locate [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.com/sindresorhus/p-locate.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.com/github/sindresorhus/p-locate)"
.PP
.RS 4
Get the first fulfilled promise that satisfies the provided testing function 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Think of it like an async version of \fR\fRArray#find\fP\fP\&.
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install p\-locate
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Here we find the first file that exists on disk, in array order\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const pathExists = require('path\-exists');
const pLocate = require('p\-locate');

const files = [
    'unicorn\&.png',
    'rainbow\&.png', // Only this one actually exists on disk
    'pony\&.png'
];

(async () => {
    const foundPath = await pLocate(files, file => pathExists(file));

    console\&.log(foundPath);
    //=> 'rainbow'
})();
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fIThe above is just an example\&. Use \fR\fRlocate-path\fP\fP if you need this\&.\fP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "pLocate(input, tester, options?)"
Returns a \fRPromise\fP that is fulfilled when \fRtester\fP resolves to \fRtrue\fP or the iterable is done, or rejects if any of the promises reject\&. The fulfilled value is the current iterable value or \fRundefined\fP if \fRtester\fP never resolved to \fRtrue\fP\&.
.SS "input"
Type: \fRIterable<Promise | unknown>\fP

.PP
An iterable of promises/values to test\&.
.SS "tester(element)"
Type: \fRFunction\fP

.PP
This function will receive resolved values from \fRinput\fP and is expected to return a \fRPromise<boolean>\fP or \fRboolean\fP\&.
.SS "options"
Type: \fRobject\fP
.SS "concurrency"
Type: \fRnumber\fP\\ Default: \fRInfinity\fP\\ Minimum: \fR1\fP

.PP
Number of concurrently pending promises returned by \fRtester\fP\&.
.SS "preserveOrder"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
Preserve \fRinput\fP order when searching\&.

.PP
Disable this to improve performance if you don't care about the order\&.
